course: dictionary
lesson: 1401
title: Carbon: an element and a gas
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Carbon is a chemical element, one of the basic building blocks of all matter. Its symbol is C. Context helps you tell which meaning fits. «Burning coal, oil and gas adds carbon dioxide to the air» is talking about a gas, not a pencil.
explain: In talk about climate, carbon is short for carbon dioxide. «Cut carbon» and «carbon footprint» are about sending less carbon dioxide into the air. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Carbon dioxide is a gas that plants take in from the air. «Breathed-out air contains less oxygen and more carbon dioxide than breathed-in air.» So when you breathe out, you send carbon dioxide back into the air.
fact: Carbon is a chemical element, with the symbol C.
fact: Carbon is found in all living things.
fact: Carbon is found in coal, in diamonds, and in the grey "lead" of a pencil, which is graphite.
fact: Carbon dioxide (CO₂) is a gas: plants take it in from the air, and animals breathe it out.
fact: Burning coal, oil and gas releases carbon dioxide, which traps heat and warms the Earth.
exercise: What is the chemical symbol for carbon? | Co | O | *C | Ca
exercise: Families talk about their «carbon footprint». What does carbon footprint mean? | A kind of diamond | *How much carbon a person or family adds to the air | The footprint left in the mud | A type of carbon pencil
exercise: «Breathed-out air contains more carbon dioxide than breathed-in air.» Which gas is breathed out? | *Carbon dioxide | Oxygen | Helium | Carbon monoxide
test: Which gas do plants take in from the air? | Carbon steel | Coal dust | Oxygen only | *Carbon dioxide
test: Which gas has no smell and is poisonous, so homes need alarms for it? | Carbon dioxide | Oxygen | *Carbon monoxide | Nitrogen
exam: Why does burning coal, oil and gas warm the Earth? | It makes the air cold | It removes all the oxygen from the air | *Because it releases carbon dioxide, which traps heat like a blanket | It turns the air into water
